import pathlib,json,collections
root=pathlib.Path('/workspace/or3-report');out=root/'stage3/census/overload-result-02d48211'
a=json.loads((out/'unit-analysis.json').read_text());d=json.loads((out/'delta.json').read_text());prov=json.loads((out/'provenance.json').read_text());cl=json.loads((out/'overloaded-value-classification.json').read_text());v=cl['results']
def loc(w):return 'src/'+w.split('/src/',1)[1] if '/src/' in w else w
def esc(s):return str(s).replace('|','\\|').replace('\n','<br>')
def fmt(f):return 'Lowered' if not f else f"{f['kind']}: {f['reason']} at {loc(f['where'])}"
def table(header,rows):return '\n'.join(['| '+' | '.join(header)+' |','| '+' | '.join(['---']*len(header))+' |']+['| '+' | '.join(esc(x) for x in row)+' |' for row in rows])
value_table=table(['Unit','Unit location','First-stop location','Overloaded expression','AST role','Classification','Parent first stop'],[[r['unit'].get('name',r['unit']['kind']),loc(r['unit']['where']),loc(r['finding']['where']),r['expression'],r['parent_role'],r['classification'],fmt(r['base'])] for r in sorted(v,key=lambda r:(r['unit'].get('name',''),r['unit']['where']))])
(out/'overloaded-values.md').write_text('# Every overloaded-value first stop at 02d48211\n\n'+value_table+'\n')
wrong=[r for r in v if r['is_callee']];right=[r for r in v if not r['is_callee']]
lines=['# Paired census: 02d48211 against 19ab1c58','','Report only. No compiler or adaptation change is included.','',f"Parent: `{prov['parent']}`. Head: `{prov['head']}`. The live optimizer branch had advanced to 28529662 when inspected; this report stays pinned to the explicitly requested 02d48211.",'',
'## Base and pairing decision','','19ab1c58 is a descendant of efe88776, but its adaptation inputs are different. `stage3/adapt/71-writable-views/adapt.cjs` changes and gains `line-map-source.cjs` and `line-map-source.json`; the adaptation README also changes. The census IR state-copy support changed as well. A fresh parent compiler and full parent census were therefore built at 19ab1c58. No old parent measurement was reused in this pair. The prior stream is read only to identify the historical 43/67 cohort members. See [base-check.json](base-check.json), [adaptation-input-diff.txt](adaptation-input-diff.txt), and [adapted-difference-from-old.json](adapted-difference-from-old.json).','',
'Both compilers were built from their own SHA and exact submodule pins. Both use the base meter instrumentation and the same single tree produced by 19ab1c58 stage3/apply.sh, from pinned TypeScript 6.0.3 `050880ce59e30b356b686bd3144efe24f875ebc8`. `LATENT_FULL=0` and `LATENT_ASSERT_NO_OUTPUT=1`. The completed headers match exactly. Both entry programs are checker-clean. The two processes ran concurrently after setup, apply and both builds completed; timing includes that overlap.','',
'## Result','', 'Only createScanner changes first stop: from `NotYet: a PostfixUnaryExpression` at `src/compiler/scanner.ts:2365:62` to `NotYet: an overloaded function as a value` at `src/compiler/scanner.ts:2190:68`. The stopped identifier is the third argument in `scanConflictMarkerTrivia(text!, pos, error)`. It is a callback value, so the guard is fail-closed and correct. The callee is scanConflictMarkerTrivia. There are no overloaded-value first stops on call callees. See [manual-review.json](manual-review.json).', '', 'createScanner remains blocked. The disappearing postfix finding is an earlier-first-stop effect, not a newly lowered unit. Total units with no lowering first stop remain 3177. All original 43 and other 67 cohort first-stop findings are unchanged from the fresh parent; the original 43 result stops are already clear on both sides, and 16 of those units lower on both sides.', '', '## Counts','',table(['Measure','Parent 19ab1c58','Head 02d48211'],[['Resolved source files',len(a['header']['sources']),len(a['header']['sources'])],['Checker diagnostics',0,0],['Units',a['unit_count'],a['unit_count']],['Attempted units',a['attempted_before'],a['attempted_after']],['Units with no lowering first stop',a['lowered_before'],a['lowered_after']],['Overload-result first stops',a['overload_before'],a['overload_after']]]),'']
counts=[]
for name,key in [('Cleared findings, no remaining finding at identity','lowered'),('Cleared findings, another reason remains','moved'),('New findings','new_findings'),('New sites','new_sites'),('Changed unit first stops','unit_first_stop_delta'),('Regressions','regressions')]:counts.append([name,len(d['raw_findings'][key]),len(d['distinct_reads'][key])])
for side in ['before','after']:
 for kind in sorted(set(d['raw_findings']['totals'][side])|set(d['distinct_reads']['totals'][side])):counts.append([side+' '+kind,d['raw_findings']['totals'][side].get(kind,0),d['distinct_reads']['totals'][side].get(kind,0)])
lines += [table(['Paired delta','Raw','Distinct'],counts),'',
'Raw findings and distinct access-chain identities use the unmodified base stage3/census/pair tool. [pair-report.md](pair-report.md) is its report; [delta.json](delta.json) retains every finding, transition, unit change, regression and panic. Newly exposed lowering first stops in already-blocked units are separated from regressions. A previously lowered attempted unit that now stops still counts as a regression even when its newly enforced value guard is correct.','',
'## Original 43-unit cohort','',f"The original 43 are tracked by source file, function name and ordinal among same-named declarations in that file. The old cohort definitions remain in the prior report. These are already part of the parent step-1 result check: {sum(r['result_stop_clear_base'] for r in a['targets'])}/43 have their result stop clear at the fresh parent, and {sum(r['result_stop_clear_head'] for r in a['targets'])}/43 at head. Units that lower: {sum(r['lowered_base'] for r in a['targets'])} parent, {sum(r['lowered_head'] for r in a['targets'])} head. The table shows the exact current first stop on each side.",'',(out/'43-units.md').read_text().strip(),'',
'## Original other 67-unit cohort','',f"{sum(r['unchanged'] for r in a['other_overload'])}/67 complete first-stop findings are unchanged from the fresh parent; {sum(not r['unchanged'] for r in a['other_overload'])} moved. Every row is retained below; MOVED rows identify all exceptions.",'',(out/'67-units.md').read_text().strip(),'',
'## Every overloaded-value first stop','',f"At head, {len(v)} units first-stop at exactly `an overloaded function as a value`, across {len(set(r['finding']['where'] for r in v))} source sites. {len(right)} units use the overloaded set as a value and the stop is fail-closed and correct. {len(wrong)} units instead use it as the callee of a call, where this fix is wrong. These judgments describe this guard at the reported source use, separately from whether the unit was already blocked.",'',
'The pinned stock TypeScript parser and checker resolve the overload symbol and record the reference AST, source context, parent role and overload declarations. Parenthesized references are followed to their enclosing expression. A reference equal to `CallExpression.expression` is a call callee. Call arguments, initializers, object properties and other expression-value uses are value uses. The Go guard and call-callee exemption are retained in [overload-value-guard.go.txt](overload-value-guard.go.txt). Full evidence for every unit is in [overloaded-value-classification.json](overloaded-value-classification.json); [overloaded-values.md](overloaded-values.md) is the standalone table.','',value_table,'','### Evidence at each distinct source site','']
seen=set()
for r in v:
 w=r['finding']['where']
 if w in seen:continue
 seen.add(w);lines += [f"`{loc(w)}`: {r['classification']}. Expression `{r['expression']}`; AST role `{r['parent_role']}`.",'','```ts',r['context'],'```','']
